<br>
<b>Madonna - Danceteria (Radio Edit) | PRIDE365 Radio Rip | 256kbps / 48kHz </b><br>
<br>
"<b>Danceteria</b>" is a song by the American singer <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Madonna</a> from her fifteenth studio album, <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confessions_II" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Confessions II</a></i> (2026). It was released on July 10, 2026, through <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warner_Records" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Warner Records</a>, as the third single from Madonna's fifteenth studio album, <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confessions_II" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Confessions II</a></i> (2026). It was written and produced by Madonna, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Watt" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Andrew Watt</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cirkut" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Cirkut</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_Price" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Stuart Price</a>, and uses an interpolation of "<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walk_on_the_Wild_Side_(Lou_Reed_song)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Walk on the Wild Side</a>" (1973), written by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lou_Reed" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Lou Reed</a>. Prior to its release, it was included in Madonna's short musical film, <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confessions_II_(film)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Confessions II</a></i> (2026).<br>
<br>
"Danceteria" is a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disco" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">disco</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electroclash" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">electroclash</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_house" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">French house</a> song. It is a tribute to the 1980s New York City downtown scene, including the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danceteria" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Danceteria</a> nightclub. In the lyrics, Madonna mentions her memories and friends from that time. The song received acclaim from music critics, who called it the album's highlight.<br>
